DIAGNOSTICS
A program that will not parse produces the name nawk was invoked under,
`Syntax error at line N', the line, a `<--' pointing at the token that
could not be used, and what was expected there.  Run-time errors are
prefixed `awk: ' whichever name was used, and are followed by the number
of the record being processed.  Both exit 1.

`exit expr' in the program sets the exit status.

NOTES
This is a third-party program, not a Mark Williams one: it was written in
1989 by Saeko and Kouichi Hirabayashi for a 16-bit Minix, deliberately to
fit 64K of text and 64K of data, which is why it fits here.  Every source
